 "brief_markdown": "# A simple calculator web app\n*Problem statement and solution brief \u00b7 draft 1 \u00b7 2026-10-25*\n\n> Each statement says where it comes from: **verified** (checked against its source) \u00b7 **research** (from the research) \u00b7 **you said** \u00b7 **recommended** (our recommendation) \u00b7 **assumption** (not confirmed). Numbers link to the references.\n\n## 1. Project overview\nA habit tracker for students.\n\n- **Users:** University students _(you said)_\n- **Context:** Self-organisation during term time. _(assumption)_\n\n## 2. Problem statement\nStudents lose track of daily habits. _(research [[1]](https://example.org/apps/0/0))_\n\n- **Who and where:** Students with irregular schedules. _(you said)_\n- **Today:** Generic habit apps with sync problems. _(research [[1]](https://example.org/apps/0/0))_\n- **Gap:** No simple offline option. _(research [[1]](https://example.org/apps/0/0))_\n- **If unresolved:** Habits are abandoned. _(assumption)_\n\n## 3. Research findings and evidence\n\n**Existing apps and user feedback**\n\n- Users complain about sync. _(research [[1]](https://example.org/apps/0/0))_\n\n**Papers and technical literature**\n\n- No usable evidence found in this domain.\n\n**Feasibility and implementations**\n\n- Static web apps can work offline. _(research [[1]](https://example.org/apps/0/0))_\n\n**Limitations of existing solutions and the opportunity**\n\n- Offline-first is underserved. _(research [[1]](https://example.org/apps/0/0))_\n\n**Evidence gaps:** pricing\n\n## 4. Proposed solution\nAn offline-first tracker removes the sync failure. _(recommended)_\n\n- **First version (MVP):** track habits \u00b7 daily reminder \u00b7 streaks\n- **Later:** sharing\n- **User journey:** open the app \u2192 tick a habit \u2192 see the streak\n- **Why this approach:** Simpler than the alternatives. _(recommended)_\n\n## 5. Functional and non-functional requirements\n\n**Functional**\n\n- Users can add and tick habits. _(you said)_\n\n**Non-functional**\n\n- Reliability: Works offline. _(recommended)_\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n\n- Ticking a habit updates the streak.\n\n## 6. Proposed architecture and technology\nA static single-page app storing data in the browser. _(recommended)_\n\n- **Frontend:** UI and storage.\n- **Data flow:** Everything stays in the browser.\n- **Technology:** Next.js (recommended): UI framework. _(recommended)_\n- **Decision:** No backend in the first version. _(recommended)_\n\n## 7. Scope and deliverables\n- **In scope:** habit tracking\n- **Out of scope:** accounts\n- **Deliverables:** web app\n\n## 8. Success criteria\n\n| Outcome | Target | How it is measured |\n|---|---|---|\n| Habits ticked per week | no target yet (no baseline) | Local usage counter. |\n\n## 9. Constraints, assumptions and risks\n- **Assumption:** No accounts.\n- **Open question:** Is mobile needed?\n- **Risk (operational):** Data loss when the browser is cleared. **Mitigation:** Export button.\n\n## 10. References\n1. [apps source 0-0](https://example.org/apps/0/0) \u00b7 Existing apps and user feedback \u00b7 verified\n\n_Statements marked verified or research cite these sources; statements marked recommended or assumption are the agents' judgement, not sourced facts._\n\n---\n## Appendix\n\n### B. Alternatives considered\n- **Differentiated product** (score 6.0/10): A solution.\n",
